Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:19:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 19/26] [Diffusion] Causal KV seam: drop the early-restore
 offer; overlap_restore is a bool (PROTOTYPE cleanup)

Early start gave no gain over the first-forward overlap: the dispatch -> begin window is ~7 ms (P1
measurements). So it is dropped:
- GPUWorker.execute_forward is back to its 9a71c04b66 form: no early offer or release around the
  forward.
- CausalDMDDenoisingStage.begin_causal_kv_early_restore is removed.
- The backend protocol docs no longer mention early_restore / release_early_restore.
- The session handle's overlap_restore is now a bool: a per-request override of the backend's
  default (on in the ReelCache bridge).

The cache seam is unchanged: restore_pending / await_restored_history at the top of
update_and_get_attention_kv, and the O(spans) layout check of a82597b232.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
